&lt;h3&gt;About the job&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Lead the system software organisation that turns complex hardware platforms into reliable Graphcore systems.&amp;nbsp;As Director of System Software, you will report to the VP of Software and turn software strategy into clear priorities, plans and outcomes. You will lead the teams delivering firmware, drivers, OpenBMC and system software QA.&amp;nbsp;Your work will shape platform bring-up, production release and long-term support across Graphcore systems. You will align technical decisions with business priorities, delivery milestones and product readiness.&amp;nbsp;You will build a strong engineering organisation, developing managers, technical leaders and engineers. You will own execution, quality and cross-functional delivery across hardware, silicon, software and product teams.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;This is a role for a leader who can think big, act fast and take responsibility for complex system outcomes.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;The team and culture&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;p&gt;System Software works close to the hardware, where small decisions can shape product reliability at scale. The team operates through clear ownership, evidence-based planning and direct technical debate.&amp;nbsp;You will lead managers and specialists across firmware, drivers, OpenBMC and QA. Decisions are made through engineering judgement, clear trade-offs and a strong focus on delivery impact.&amp;nbsp;You will be expected to speak up, challenge assumptions and help resolve issues across hardware and software boundaries. Pace matters, but so do maintainability, security and long term quality.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;What we’re looking for&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;p&gt;· A strong track record leading system software teams across closely coupled hardware and software programmes.&lt;br&gt;· Experience managing managers or multiple technical teams, with clear ownership of delivery outcomes.&lt;br&gt;· Proven ability to build, coach and develop engineering leaders through change and technical uncertainty.&lt;br&gt;· Strong judgement across planning, resourcing, dependencies, risk and production release readiness.&lt;br&gt;· Experience embedding validation, automated testing, hardware-in-the-loop testing and clear release criteria.&lt;br&gt;· Credible technical breadth across firmware, drivers, OpenBMC, QA or related low-level software domains.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;While we have outlined a set of requirements, we value transferable skills and diverse experiences. We also welcome engineers returning to the profession after a career break, including through returnship routes.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;Benefits&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;p&gt;· Flexible working: Balance your work and personal life with greater flexibility&lt;br&gt;· Generous leave: Take time to rest, recharge and enjoy life outside of work&amp;nbsp;&lt;br&gt;· Retirement planning support: Up to 5% matched pension&lt;br&gt;· Phantom equity: Share in Graphcore’s success&lt;br&gt;· Workplace experience: Enjoy thoughtfully designed office spaces for collaboration, with free food and an on-site barista to support your day&lt;br&gt;· Peace of mind protection: Income protection and life assurance to provide financial security for you and your loved ones&lt;br&gt;· Electric Vehicle Scheme: Choose an electric vehicle and lease it through salary sacrifice&lt;br&gt;· Flexible benefits: Tailor your benefits package with a choice of additional options, including private medical insurance and dental cover&lt;br&gt;· Optional benefits: Dental cover, health cash plan, private medical insurance, cycle to work scheme, give as you earn&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;We welcome people from all backgrounds and experiences and are committed to building an inclusive environment where everyone can do their best work.&lt;br&gt;We’re an equal opportunity employer and recognise that everyone brings different strengths and perspectives. If you need any adjustments during the interview process, just let us know - we’re happy to support you.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;Join the Team at Graphcore&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Graphcore is one of the world’s leading innovators in Artificial Intelligence compute. It is developing hardware, software and systems infrastructure that will unlock the next generation of AI breakthroughs and power the widespread adoption of AI solutions across every industry.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;As part of the SoftBank Group, Graphcore is a member of an elite family of companies responsible for some of the world’s most transformative technologies. Together, they share a bold vision: to enable Artificial Super Intelligence and ensure its benefits are accessible to everyone.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Graphcore’s teams are drawn from diverse backgrounds and bring a broad range of skills and perspectives. A melting pot of AI research specialists, silicon designers, software engineers and systems architects, Graphcore brings together deep expertise to solve complex problems and deliver meaningful progress in AI compute.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;If you want to lead the system software organisation behind Graphcore’s next generation platforms, we’d love to hear from you. Apply now to be part of the journey.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;Sponsorship&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Applicants must have the legal right to work in the UK. Unfortunately, we are unable to provide visa sponsorship or support visa applications for this role.&lt;/p&gt;<p>Find <a href="https://www.arbeitnow.co.uk">Jobs in United Kingdom</a> on Arbeitnow</a>

&lt;div class=&quot;content-intro&quot;&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;500M+ downloads. 80M+ monthly users. A decade of building – and we’re still accelerating.&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Flo is the world’s #1 health &amp;amp; fitness app worldwide on a mission to build a better future for female health. Backed by a $200M investment led by General Atlantic, we became the first product of our kind to reach a $1B valuation in 2024 – and we’re not slowing down.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;With 7M paid subscribers and the highest-rated experience in the App Store’s health category, we’ve spent 10 years earning trust at scale. Now, we’re building the next generation of digital health – AI-powered, privacy-first, clinically backed – to help our users know their body better.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;The job&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;h1&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Principal Infrastructure Engineer&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h1&gt;
&lt;p&gt;More than 80 million women open Flo every month to understand their bodies and their health. Every one of those sessions runs on infrastructure we build, and the data behind it is as personal as data gets. Keeping that fast and private at this scale is the job.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Velocity runs the platform that every Flo engineer builds on: Kubernetes on AWS, the data stores behind our services, and the golden paths that let product teams ship without needing to be infrastructure experts. We treat our internal developers as our customers. You will:&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Own the foundations:&lt;/strong&gt; Design and run the Kubernetes and data infrastructure behind 80 million monthly active users, and make it boring in the best sense.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Turn expertise into self-service:&lt;/strong&gt; Take what you know about running clusters and databases well, and build it into the defaults so product teams get it for free.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;What You Will Do&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Kubernetes at scale:&lt;/strong&gt; Architect and evolve our EKS estate: cluster lifecycle and upgrades, networking, autoscaling, workload isolation, and the Helm and Terraform that deploy onto it.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Data infrastructure:&lt;/strong&gt; Shape how our services use PostgreSQL, DynamoDB and Kafka. Set the patterns for provisioning, access, backup, failover and capacity, so teams aren&#39;t solving these problems one service at a time.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Golden paths:&lt;/strong&gt; Build self-service tooling and Terraform modules that give product teams autonomy without sacrificing stability or security.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Reliability:&lt;/strong&gt; Lead resilience work, including business continuity planning, disaster recovery testing and a sustainable on-call rotation.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Privacy at scale:&lt;/strong&gt; Support the infrastructure behind privacy features such as our TIME-recognised &quot;Anonymous Mode&quot;, and keep us SOC2, ISO 27001 and ISO 27701 certified while handling some of the most sensitive data there is.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Observability:&lt;/strong&gt; Make sure metrics, logs and traces tell us something is wrong before our users do.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;What You Bring&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Experience:&lt;/strong&gt; Many years in infrastructure, platform, SRE or DevOps roles running high-traffic, distributed systems in production. You have operated at Principal or Staff scope, setting direction across teams as well as delivering.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Kubernetes depth:&lt;/strong&gt; You have run Kubernetes in production for real workloads, ideally EKS. You can explain what happens between kubectl apply and a pod serving traffic, and you have debugged it when it didn&#39;t.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Data infrastructure awareness:&lt;/strong&gt; You understand how PostgreSQL, DynamoDB and Kafka behave under load and when they fail: connection limits, replication lag, hot partitions, consumer lag, retention. You don&#39;t need to have been a DBA, but you know what good looks like and when to ask for help.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;AWS and infrastructure as code:&lt;/strong&gt; Strong AWS knowledge and fluent Terraform. Coding experience in Go or Python is a plus.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Communication:&lt;/strong&gt; A doc-first habit, and the ability to bring distributed product teams with you.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;AI first: you will have seen the impact AI automation is having on development teams and the software delivery lifecycle, and have strong ideas on how infrastructure should support it.&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Bonus Points&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Hardening infrastructure for high-compliance or security-sensitive environments (HIPAA, SOC 2, PCI).&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Running managed data services in AWS (RDS, Aurora, MSK, DynamoDB) at scale, including migrations and major version upgrades.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Scaling consumer platforms with millions of concurrent users.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Certifications such as AWS Certified Solutions Architect Professional, CKA or CKS.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Why Join Flo?&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;High impact:&lt;/strong&gt; Flo is used by 1 in 4 women aged 18–44 in the US, and has raised $200M to build what comes next.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Autonomy:&lt;/strong&gt; We hire experts and trust them to deliver.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Modern stack at scale:&lt;/strong&gt; EKS, Terraform, Kafka, PostgreSQL, DynamoDB and Sentry, serving more than 80 million people a month.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;content-pay-transparency&quot;&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;pay-input&quot;&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;title&quot;&gt;Annual Salary Range (ranges may vary based on skills and experience)&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;pay-range&quot;&gt;&lt;span&gt;£130,000&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class=&quot;divider&quot;&gt;&amp;mdash;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span&gt;£150,000 GBP&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;content-conclusion&quot;&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;How we work&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;We’re a mission-led, product-driven team. We move fast, stay focused and take ownership – from brief to build to impact. Debate is encouraged. Decisions are shared. We care about craft, ship with purpose, and always raise the bar.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;You’ll be working with people who take their work seriously, not themselves. It takes commitment, resilience, and the drive to keep going when things get tough. Because better health outcomes are worth it.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;What you&#39;ll get&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;We support impact with meaningful reward. Here’s what that looks like:&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Competitive salary and annual reviews&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Opportunity to participate in Flo’s performance incentive scheme&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Paid holiday, sick leave, and female health leave&lt;/li&gt;
